{"name":"Sea Serpent","hex":"#4bc7cf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea serpent","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of sea monster resembling a snake or dragon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_serpent"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea serpent","blocks":[{"text":"A sea serpent is a type of sea monster described in various mythologies and religious texts. Famous sea serpents include: the Mesopotamian Tiamat, Ugaritic Yam and Tannin, Judaic Leviathan and Rahab, ancient Greek Cetus, Echidna, Hydra and Scylla, Vedic Vritra and Surasa, and the Norse Jörmungandr, etc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Sea_serpent.jpg/330px-Sea_serpent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_serpent"},{"title":"Sea Serpent (clipper)","blocks":[{"text":"Sea Serpent was an 1850 extreme clipper that sailed in the San Francisco trade, the China trade, and the transatlantic lumber trade. She was one of the longest lived clippers, with a service life of 36 years and 5 months."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/SEA_SERPENT_%28Ship%29_%28c112-02-25%29.jpg/330px-SEA_SERPENT_%28Ship%29_%28c112-02-25%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_Serpent_(clipper)"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Reggio_calabria_museo_nazionale_mosaico_da_kaulon.jpg/330px-Reggio_calabria_museo_nazionale_mosaico_da_kaulon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Reggio_calabria_museo_nazionale_mosaico_da_kaulon.jpg/330px-Reggio_calabria_museo_nazionale_mosaico_da_kaulon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mosaic of a cetus sea serpent of Greek mythology","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AReggio_calabria_museo_nazionale_mosaico_da_kaulon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Lee_Henry1883-Unmasked-p066-seaserpent-egede.png/500px-Lee_Henry1883-Unmasked-p066-seaserpent-egede.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Lee_Henry1883-Unmasked-p066-seaserpent-egede.png/1280px-Lee_Henry1883-Unmasked-p066-seaserpent-egede.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Lee_Henry1883-Unmasked-p066-seaserpent-egede.png/500px-Lee_Henry1883-Unmasked-p066-seaserpent-egede.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALee_Henry1883-Unmasked-p066-seaserpent-egede.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Hans_Egede_1734_sea_serpent.jpg/500px-Hans_Egede_1734_sea_serpent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Hans_Egede_1734_sea_serpent.jpg/500px-Hans_Egede_1734_sea_serpent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHan